From f18c682000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simone Primarosa <simone.primarosa@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 10:48:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat: split scale-up across flavors into sub-group podsets

When an elastic workload scales up, the scheduler assigns flavors per PodSet. If a worker group's original flavor lacks sufficient available capacity in the ClusterQueue, the entire scale-up request is blocked even when alternative flavors have ample capacity. Workload slices cannot split an existing PodSet across different flavors because all pods in a PodSet share the same flavor assignment.

Split elastic worker groups into sub-group PodSets with deterministic numeric suffixes upon scheduler refusal. Each split entry preserves the original group's template and properties while allowing independent flavor assignment and ungate tracking. Update workload slicing, flavor assignment, preemption scoring, and pod admission ungating to reconcile split entries transparently without altering the parent job specification.
